From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: do not force the build-host architecture

The release flags unconditionally select -march=native and -mtune=native.
Besides overriding distribution policy, GCC cannot translate "native" into a
valid RISC-V ISA string under the approved QEMU user build route. Leave target
selection to the openEuler RVA23 compiler flags while preserving the remaining
upstream release options.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of dictpopup 0.3.2 CMakeLists.txt
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -87 +87 @@
-set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS_RELEASE "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS_RELEASE} -Ofast -flto -march=native -mtune=native -g -fno-omit-frame-pointer")
+set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS_RELEASE "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS_RELEASE} -Ofast -flto -g -fno-omit-frame-pointer")
-- 
2.50.1
